533790 true] [17592186129719 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533790 true] [17592186129719 1145 "Given a function in the form $f(x)=A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(Bx+C)+D,$ the period $T$ is given by $\\frac{2\\pi }{B}.$\n\nIn our case, we have that $B=\\frac{5}{3}.$ Therefore, the period is $\\frac{2\\pi }{(\\frac{5}{3})}=\\frac{6\\pi }{5}.$" 13194139533790 true] [17592186251339 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251340 13194139533790 true] [17592186251339 1089 "q-10379" 13194139533790 true] [17592186251339 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533790 true] [17592186251339 1100 "Find the range of the function $y=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-2.$" 13194139533790 true] [17592186251339 1113 #uuid "6b211722-74ca-5ce0-9e29-ed681235d5e8" 13194139533790 true] [17592186251339 1145 "The range of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $2$ and then subtracting $2,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\le 1 \\\\  & -2\\le 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)\\le 2 \\\\  & -4\\le 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4x)-2\\le 0 \\\\  & -4\\le y\\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [-4,0].$" 13194139533790 true] [17592186251340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251341 13194139533790 true] [17592186251340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251342 13194139533790 true] [17592186251340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251343 13194139533790 true] [17592186251340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251344 13194139533790 true] [17592186251340 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251345 13194139533790 true] [17592186251340 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533790 true] [17592186251340 1041 "selection" 13194139533790 true] [17592186251340 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251341 13194139533790 true] [17592186251340 1110 #uuid "af264a72-7d28-58e0-bdfc-f3f91226bcba" 13194139533790 true] [17592186251341 1034 "y\\in [-4,0]" 13194139533790 true] [17592186251341 1103 #